  "id": "gray-ramus",
  "term": "gray ramus",
  "definition": "In this packet, the gray ramus is the lumbar nerve pathway from which postganglionic sympathetic nerve activity was recorded. It is described as part of the sympathetic output to the hind limb that becomes active during reflex responses to skeletal muscle contraction.",
